[{"text":"dr Er(n,s,c)→ Er(n-1, s+r, c+1); on each page r=2,3, the maximal rank the dimensions allow is taken. The pages are processed in order.","section":"The rule as we understood it"},{"text":"The grammar gives stem=4(indices)-\\#λ, that is, c stem+s mod 4. Hence an arrow “colour +1” is possible only for r2mod4: d2, d6, d10, The variant “colour -1” gives no differentials at all, and in it π44 keeps four classes, whereas the lecture says it is empty.","section":"The rule as we understood it"},{"text":"On page r the possible arrows line up into chains x→ y→ z→ with decreasing n. The maximal total rank on a chain is determined uniquely, but which classes die is not: a middle class can be either a target or a source. “low” fills a chain starting from the end with the smaller n, “high” from the end with the larger. For n≤149 the two variants differ only here:","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"only in “low”:","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"from (s, c) · to (s, c) · rank","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π42 (7, 2) · π41 (9, 3) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π52 (9, 2) · π51 (11, 3) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π62 (11, 2) · π61 (13, 3) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π72 (13, 2) · π71 (15, 3) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π75 (6, 2) · π74 (8, 3) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π78 (7, 2) · π77 (9, 3) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π79 (7, 3) · π78 (9, 4) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π82 (15, 2) · π81 (17, 3) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π85 (8, 2) · π84 (10, 3) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π86 (7, 2) · π85 (9, 3) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π88 (9, 2) · π87 (11, 3) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π89 (9, 3) · π88 (11, 4) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π90 (10, 5) · π89 (12, 6) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π92 (17, 2) · π91 (19, 3) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π93 (8, 2) · π92 (10, 3) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π94 (8, 3) · π93 (10, 4) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π95 (10, 2) · π94 (12, 3) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π97 (9, 3) · π96 (11, 4) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π98 (9, 4) · π97 (11, 5) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π98 (11, 2) · π97 (13, 3) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π99 (10, 6) · π98 (12, 7) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π99 (11, 3) · π98 (13, 4) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π100 (12, 5) · π99 (14, 6) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π102 (8, 3) · π101 (10, 4) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π102 (19, 2) · π101 (21, 3) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π109 (8, 2) · π108 (10, 3) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"},{"text":"d2 · π108 (11, 4) · π107 (13, 5) · 1","section":"Where the rule is ambiguous"}]